msgstr "`-x` (минус)"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/01-intro-syntax-types.md:1311
msgid "comparisons: `==`, `!=`, `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`"
msgstr "сравнения: `==`, `!=`, `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/01-intro-syntax-types.md:1314
msgid "9 (last)"
msgstr "9 (последен)"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/01-intro-syntax-types.md:1316
msgid "Operators of the same priority run from left to right - except `**`, which runs from right to left. When in doubt, add brackets: they also make the code easier to read."
msgstr "Операторите с еднакъв приоритет се изпълняват отляво надясно - освен `**`, който се изпълнява отдясно наляво. Когато се съмнявате, сложете скоби: така и кодът се чете по-лесно."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/01-intro-syntax-types.md:1328
msgid "**How an expression is evaluated:** [1. Precedence](../animations/expressionEvaluation.html#1){target=\"_blank\"}, [2. Brackets](../animations/expressionEvaluation.html#2){target=\"_blank\"}, [3. `**` and minus](../animations/expressionEvaluation.html#3){target=\"_blank\"}, [4. `//` and `%`](../animations/expressionEvaluation.html#4){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Как се изчислява израз:** [1. Приоритет](../animations/expressionEvaluation.html#1){target=\"_blank\"}, [2. Скоби](../animations/expressionEvaluation.html#2){target=\"_blank\"}, [3. `**` и минус](../animations/expressionEvaluation.html#3){target=\"_blank\"}, [4. `//` и `%`](../animations/expressionEvaluation.html#4){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/01-intro-syntax-types.md:1335
msgid "Comparison operators"
msgstr "Оператори за сравнение"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/01-intro-syntax-types.md:1339
msgid "equal"
msgstr "равно"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/01-intro-syntax-types.md:1340
msgid "not equal"
msgstr "различно"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/01-intro-syntax-types.md:1341
msgid "less (or equal)"
msgstr "по-малко (или равно)"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/01-intro-syntax-types.md:1342
msgid "greater (or equal)"
msgstr "по-голямо (или равно)"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/01-intro-syntax-types.md:1344
msgid "`=` gives a name, `==` compares. The result is a `bool`. Comparisons can be **chained** - like `BETWEEN` in SQL:"
msgstr "`=` дава име, `==` сравнява. Резултатът е `bool`. Сравненията могат да се **свързват във верига** - като `BETWEEN` в SQL:"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/01-intro-syntax-types.md:1355
msgid "Logical operators"
msgstr "Логически оператори"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/01-intro-syntax-types.md:1357
msgid "`and`, `or` and `not` combine conditions - in small letters, as words:"
msgstr "`and`, `or` и `not` комбинират условия - с малки букви, като думи:"

#. box title
#: site/lectures/01-intro-syntax-types.md:1367
msgid "`&` and `|` are not `and` and `or`"
msgstr "`&` и `|` не са `and` и `or`"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/01-intro-syntax-types.md:1368
msgid "In SAS, `&` and `|` mean AND and OR. In Python they are different (bit) operators. pandas uses them for conditions on whole columns (session 15) - but for single values, write `and`, `or`, `not`."
msgstr "В SAS `&` и `|` означават AND и OR. В Python те са други (побитови) оператори. pandas ги използва за условия върху цели колони (занятие 15) - но за отделни стойности пишете `and`, `or`, `not`."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/01-intro-syntax-types.md:1373
msgid "`if` with conditions, and the details of `and` / `or`, come in session 2."
msgstr "`if` с условия и подробностите за `and` / `or` идват в занятие 2."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/01-intro-syntax-types.md:1376
msgid "**How an expression is evaluated:** [5. Chained comparisons](../animations/expressionEvaluation.html#5){target=\"_blank\"}, [6. `and` / `or`](../animations/expressionEvaluation.html#6){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Как се изчислява израз:** [5. Верига от сравнения](../animations/expressionEvaluation.html#5){target=\"_blank\"}, [6. `and` / `or`](../animations/expressionEvaluation.html#6){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/01-intro-syntax-types.md:1381
msgid "Operators on strings"
msgstr "Оператори върху strings"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/01-intro-syntax-types.md:1383
msgid "`+` joins two strings (like `||` in SQL and SAS), and `*` repeats a string:"
msgstr "`+` съединява два strings (като `||` в SQL и SAS), а `*` повтаря string:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/01-intro-syntax-types.md:1392
msgid "Python does not mix types for you - \"apples with oranges\" is an error:"
msgstr "Python не смесва типовете вместо вас - \"ябълки с круши\" е грешка:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/01-intro-syntax-types.md:1402
msgid "The fix is an explicit conversion, `\"Stage \" + str(3)` (section 12), or an f-string (section 13)."
msgstr "Решението е явно преобразуване, `\"Stage \" + str(3)` (раздел 12), или f-string (раздел 13)."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/01-intro-syntax-types.md:1406
msgid "**How an expression is evaluated:** [7. Mixed types](../animations/expressionEvaluation.html#7){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Как се изчислява израз:** [7. Смесени типове](../animations/expressionEvaluation.html#7){target=\"_blank\"}"

